From: PLC110 TWRP device tree
Subject: [PATCH] Do not block forever on a declared but unregistered IBootControl

Recovery ships a VINTF fragment for android.hardware.boot so that
update_engine_sideload and fastbootd can use the vendor HAL, but the HAL
binary lives on /vendor.  In fastbootd mode TWRP does not mount /vendor, so
the declared instance is never registered and the FastbootDevice constructor
blocked before it created the USB transport - which made the host see no
device at all:

  I:进入 Fastbootd 模式
  I servicemanager: Caller(pid=980,...) Since 'android.hardware.boot.IBootControl/default'
     could not be found trying to start it as a lazy AIDL service.
  E init: Control message: Could not find 'aidl/android.hardware.boot.IBootControl/default'
     for ctl.interface_start from pid: 434
  I ServiceManagerCppClient: Waiting for service 'android.hardware.boot.IBootControl/default'
     on '/dev/binder'...          <- and it stays here
  I init: Service 'fastbootd' (pid 980) received signal 9

AServiceManager_waitForService() never returns while a declared instance is
missing, and AServiceManager_getService() is no better: it is documented as
"this polls 5s" and calls the same blocking getService() underneath, so
polling it turned the hang into 50 x 5s.

Poll AServiceManager_checkService() - the only non-blocking lookup - for at
most five seconds and continue without the HAL.  Every consumer handles a null
client: fastbootd reports an empty slot suffix and keeps serving the partitions
it can reach, and update_engine_sideload only runs in normal recovery mode
where the device tree starts the HAL before it is needed.

diff --git a/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp b/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp
diff --git a/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp b/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp
index 7aab5b4..f702800 100644
--- a/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp
+++ b/boot/aidl/client/BootControlClient.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <aidl/android/hardware/boot/IBootControl.h>
 #include <android-base/logging.h>
 #include <android/binder_ibinder.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include <android/binder_manager.h>
 #include <android/hardware/boot/1.0/IBootControl.h>
 #include <android/hardware/boot/1.1/IBootControl.h>
@@ -406,15 +407,34 @@ std::unique_ptr<BootControlClient> BootControlClient::WaitForService() {
     const auto instance_name =
             std::string(::aidl::android::hardware::boot::IBootControl::descriptor) + "/default";
     if (AServiceManager_isDeclared(instance_name.c_str())) {
-        auto module = ::aidl::android::hardware::boot::IBootControl::fromBinder(
-                ndk::SpAIBinder(AServiceManager_waitForService(instance_name.c_str())));
-        if (module == nullptr) {
-            LOG(ERROR) << "AIDL " << instance_name
-                       << " is declared but waitForService returned nullptr.";
-            return nullptr;
-        }
-        LOG(INFO) << "Using AIDL version of IBootControl";
-        return std::make_unique<BootControlClientAidl>(module);
+        // Recovery declares the HAL from its own VINTF fragment while the vendor
+        // implementation lives on /vendor.  fastbootd mode does not mount /vendor,
+        // so the instance can stay unregistered forever, and waitForService() -
+        // which only returns once *some* instance is served - blocked inside the
+        // FastbootDevice constructor, before the USB transport was created.
+        // Poll with the non-blocking checkService() for a moment and continue
+        // without the HAL instead; every caller copes with a null client
+        // (fastbootd then reports an empty slot suffix).  Note AServiceManager_-
+        // getService() is not an option: it is the blocking one, it polls for 5s.
+        AIBinder* binder = nullptr;
+        for (int attempt = 0; attempt < 50 && binder == nullptr; ++attempt) {
+            binder = AServiceManager_checkService(instance_name.c_str());
+            if (binder == nullptr) usleep(100 * 1000);
+        }
+        if (binder == nullptr) {
+            LOG(WARNING) << "AIDL " << instance_name
+                         << " is declared but never registered; continuing without it.";
+        } else {
+            auto module = ::aidl::android::hardware::boot::IBootControl::fromBinder(
+                    ndk::SpAIBinder(binder));
+            if (module == nullptr) {
+                LOG(ERROR) << "AIDL " << instance_name
+                           << " is declared but checkService returned a broken binder.";
+                return nullptr;
+            }
+            LOG(INFO) << "Using AIDL version of IBootControl";
+            return std::make_unique<BootControlClientAidl>(module);
+        }
     }
     LOG(INFO) << "AIDL IBootControl not available, falling back to HIDL.";
 
